        "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 20 at 1:30AM MST until October 22 at 10:00PM MST by NWS Tucson AZ",
        "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of Southeast Arizona, including the following\nareas, Galiuro and Pinaleno Mountains, Upper Gila River Valley and\nWhite Mountains of Graham and Greenlee Counties.\n\n* WHEN...From late Wednesday morning through Thursday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- A strong weather system approaching the area will bring scattered\nshowers and thunderstorms on Wednesday and widespread showers and\nscattered thunderstorms on Thursday. Moderate to locally heavy\nrainfall both days with Thursday having the higher potential for\nlocalized rainfall rates of 1 to 2 inches per hour.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
