        "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 20 at 12:37AM MST until October 22 at 11:00PM MST by NWS Flagstaff AZ",
        "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...All of northern and central Arizona.\n\n* WHEN...From late tonight through Thursday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flash flooding will be possible in creeks, normally dry\nwashes, swimming holes, and over recently burned areas. Low-water\ncrossings may be flooded.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- An upper-level trough will bring a deep surge of subtropical and\ntropical moisture into our region. Showers and thunderstorms will\ndevelop across much of northern and central Arizona early\nWednesday morning and continue through Thursday evening. Stronger\nthunderstorms will bring threats of Flash Flooding, while more\nprolonged rainfall could lead to elevated flow in streams,\nrivers, and washes.\n- Additional information is available at weather.gov/flagstaff.",
